course: dictionary
lesson: 2822
title: Words for songs and poems
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A ditty is a short, simple song or poem, often cheerful or funny. You can work out this meaning from the words around it. Ratty in The Wind in the Willows makes up little songs, and one of them is called «Ducks' Ditty».
explain: Read the song itself: «All along the backwater, / Through the rushes tall, / Ducks are a-dabbling, / Up tails all!» The lines are short, they rhyme (tall and all), and they bounce along. That tells you what a ditty sounds like.
explain: Context can also show you the mood. Toad sings boastful ditties about himself, so these ditties are bragging songs. Always test your meaning: if you swap in «song» and the sentence still makes sense, your guess is probably right.
fact: A ditty is a short, simple song or poem.
fact: A ditty is often cheerful or funny.
fact: «Ducks' Ditty» is a short song that Ratty makes up in The Wind in the Willows.
fact: Toad sings boastful ditties, which means songs that show off about himself.
fact: In music lessons, a ditty is an easy tune to learn.
exercise: Ratty makes up a little song called «Ducks' Ditty». What is a ditty? | A sharp tool for digging | A kind of duck | *A short, simple song or poem | A long, serious story
exercise: The Ducks' Ditty has lines that rhyme. Which pair of words rhymes in the song? | Ducks and rushes | Water and bank | *Tall and all | Up and tails
exercise: «Up tails all!» is a line from the Ducks' Ditty. What does it describe? | Ratty sleeping on the bank | A boat racing across the river | *Ducks tipping their heads under the water with their tails up to nibble plants | A duck's wing flapping in the wind
test: In music lessons, what is a ditty? | A type of instrument | A difficult exam | *An easy tune to learn | A long piece for an orchestra
test: Toad sings boastful ditties about himself. What does boastful suggest? | Lost and tired | Cheerful about the weather | *Bragging and showing off | Shy and quiet
exam: «Ducks' Ditty» is a short, simple song about ducks, so what kind of thing is it? | A river | A recipe | A paragraph | *A ditty
